From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Synthex Linux Team <kernel@getsynthex.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] synthex-0005-rust-for-linux.patch

Enable Rust for Linux support on x86_64.

Rust has been upstream in the Linux kernel since v6.1 and is
stabilised for production use as of v6.14. This patch enables Rust
support in the default x86_64 kernel configuration so that `make
defconfig` produces a Rust-ready kernel out of the box.

Enabled Rust subsystems:
  - Core Rust support (CONFIG_RUST)
  - PHYLIB abstractions — Rust bindings for network PHY drivers
  - ASIX PHY driver — Rust-based Ethernet PHY driver
  - Sample PHY driver — Rust-based PHY driver template

Build requirements:
  - rustc >= 1.80.0 with rust-src and rust-std components
  - bindgen for generating FFI bindings
  - cargo (for Rust module builds)

Signed-off-by: Synthex Linux Team <kernel@getsynthex.org>
---
 arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig b/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
--- a/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +0,0 @@
+# Rust for Linux — memory-safe kernel modules
+CONFIG_RUST=y
+CONFIG_RUST_BUILD_ASSERT_ALLOW=y
+CONFIG_RUST_PHYLIB_ABSTRACTIONS=y
+CONFIG_RUST_DRIVER_ASIX=m
+CONFIG_RUST_DRIVER_PHY=m
-- 
2.45.0
